---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Current graduate student in UCSF’s department of Radiology and Biomedical imaging interested in scientific computing and machine learning for healthcare applications.
    Interested in research, image processing pipeline development, and building the next generation of imaging technologies. I'm a creative and determined problem solver
    and a constantly curious individual who is always down to learn and collaborate.

  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Master of Science in Biomedical Imaging"
      subtitle="2025 to 2026 at University of California, San Francisco, San Francisco, CA"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Bachelor of Science in Physics and Mathematics"
      subtitle="2017 to 2022 at University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Graduate Research Assistant"
      subtitle="From January 2026 to present at University of California, San Francisco"
    >
      • Conducting thesis research under the supervision of Dr. Jessica Scholey from UCSF’s Department of Radiation Oncology.
Working on using Python to develop a set of post-processing tools for ensuring anatomical accuracy of synthetic CT
generated using convolutional neural networks for MRI-only workflows.
• Managing data from a large number of subjects and studies across MRI and CT scans as well as generated CT images.
Leveraging imaging libraries such as OpenCV, scikit-image, and ANTSpy among others. Working with both traditional
image registration and processing methods as well as implementing neural-network based registration to establish
robustness against edge cases in image reconstruction.
• Designed thesis experiment and developing toolset for synthetic CT quality assurance using various image similarity
metrics.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Course Coordinator/Student Affairs Specialist"
      subtitle="From June 2023 to August 2025 at University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"
    >
     • Maintained a large database of course materials, using the Microsoft suite (Excel, Word) and Google suite (Sheets, Docs,
Slides). Processed and analyzed data in preparation for an upcoming paper I have authored.
• Updated the main course website weekly, maintained other course pages and data such as Canvas, Gradescope, Piazza,
and PrairieLearn, sent course announcements, and processed and posted grades.
• Handled requests for extensions, regrades, accommodations, and excused absences for a course of approximately 800
students. Processed regrades and worked with students to build plans for completing work
• Maintained the staff office and coordinated communications with building management, handled reimbursements and
course registration add/drop overrides.
• Coordinated between multiple departments and institutions to facilitate the formation of a persistent computer-based
testing facility for College of Engineering use.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Undergraduate Research Assistant"
      subtitle="From May 2019 to May 2022 at University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"
    >
      • Investigated techniques of star-galaxy separation under the supervision of Dr. Eric Bell.
• Developed a two-point galaxy autocorrelation function in order to better characterize substructure of background
galaxies.
• Used Python to analyze large datasets, working with tools such as NumPy, Astropy, and matplotlib.
• Communicated results and visualizations in group meetings.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Certifications</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>
      <a href="#" target="_blank"> Basic Life Support certification through American Red Cross</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>Python Scripting</li>
    <li>C++</li>
    <li>Javascript</li>
    <li>R</li>
    <li>HTML</li>
    <li>SQL</li>
    <li>Docker</li>
    <li>PyTorch</li>
    <li>TensorFlow</li>
    <li>CUDA</li>
    <li>OpenCV</li>
    <li>Node.js</li>
    <li>ImageJ</li>
    <li>CONN</li>
    <li>AMIDE</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
